      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 85.68, 639.982, 539.924, 666.066 ],
      "font" : "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular",
      "font size" : 10.909,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "1. In [2], the authors compute the ample cone for Hilbert modular surface, by constructing partial Hasse invariants and studying intersection theory on the surface directly.",
      "kids" : [ ]
    }, {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 85.68, 582.262, 539.914, 625.161 ],
      "font" : "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular",
      "font size" : 10.909,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "2. In [40], the authors conjectured the ampleness criterion for U(2)/Hilbert/quaternionic Shimura varieties. They studied the geometric description of Goren–Oort strata and proved the necessity part of the criterion.",
      "kids" : [ ]
    }, {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 85.68, 540.742, 539.575, 566.825 ],
      "font" : "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular",
      "font size" : 10.909,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "3. In [45], the author proved the ampleness criterion conjectured by [40], by computing the intersection numbers using the description of strata.",
      "kids" : [ ]
    }, {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 85.68, 499.222, 539.924, 525.425 ],
      "font" : "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular",
      "font size" : 10.909,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "4. In the unpublished paper [5], the authors proposed a suﬃciency criterion for ampleness for Hodge type Shimura varieties. However, their bound is known to be not sharp.",
      "kids" : [ ]
    } ]
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 6,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 436.812, 539.936, 481.108 ],
    "font" : "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "We know very little about the ampleness criterion beyond the above cases, especially when the group G is not type A1. The main diﬃculty is that the stratiﬁcation of the ﬂag space is usually very complicated, and computing intersection numbers (LY(λ) · C) with a complete curve C ⊆ Y is non-trivial."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 7,
